//
// A numeric inner loop, for timing the Cranelift JIT against the Tier 0
// interpreter on one and the same program. The body is the shape the tier
// compiles best: an integer in, a straight line of literal arithmetic, and
// nothing left behind.
//
// `times` pushes the iteration index before each run of the body. Bund's
// binary words take their right operand first, so `x 3 -` is 3 - x, and the
// chain turns the index x into -(x + 3) before `drop` discards it. The loop
// keeps nothing it computes; the README says what it is for.
//
// N comes from `--n <int>`, ten million when absent:
//   bund2 kernel.bund --n 1000000
//   ./kernel --n 1000000
//

args.parse :n ?key
{ drop 10000000 }
{ :n get car convert.to_int }
?true*

dup { 1 + 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 + 6 - 7 + 8 + 9 - drop } times
print " iterations" println
